{"name":"Baker’s Dream","hex":"#c98f70","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"baker","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person who bakes and sells bread, cakes and similar items.","A portable oven for baking."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/baker"},{"term":"dream","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Imaginary events seen in the mind while sleeping.","A hope or wish."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To see imaginary events in one's mind while sleeping.","To hope, to wish."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dream"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dream","blocks":[{"text":"A dream is a succession of images, dynamic scenes and situations, ideas, emotions, and sensations that usually occur involuntarily in the mind during certain stages of sleep. Humans generally spend more than two hours dreaming per night, and each dream lasts around 5–20 minutes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/A_dream_%28BM_1868%2C0808.9057%29.jpg/330px-A_dream_%28BM_1868%2C0808.9057%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dream","wikidata":"Q36348"},{"title":"Baker","blocks":[{"text":"A baker is a tradesperson who bakes and sometimes sells breads and other products made of flour by using an oven or other concentrated heat source. The place where a baker works is called a bakery."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/USS_John_C._Stennis_baker.jpg/330px-USS_John_C._Stennis_baker.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baker","wikidata":"Q160131"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Raja_Ravi_Varma%2C_Usha%27s_Dream_%28oleographic_print%29.jpg/500px-Raja_Ravi_Varma%2C_Usha%27s_Dream_%28oleographic_print%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","sr